== CANON-20 / ADR-0008: `in` (level 11) binds tighter than the relational
== operators (level 12), so `X in 1..9 = Flag` means `(X in 1..9) = Flag`. The
== test is shape-discriminating: the wrong grouping `X in 1..(9 = Flag)` would
== compare the Integer 9 with a Bool and fail semantic analysis.
Module PrecedenceInRelational

Main :
    X Integer := 4
    Flag Bool := True
    B Bool := X in 1..9 = Flag
    PutLn(B)
;
